From: Project Luma <noreply@project-luma.local>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 22:55:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] tee: qseecom: isolate stock heaps from global SCM

The FP6 requires stock-compatible whole-pool SHM Bridge registrations for its
QSEECom TA and apps heaps. Registering those heaps on the global SCM device
also redirected unrelated SCM clients through the TA pool and produced Adreno
GMU timeouts during physical testing.

Make TZ memory allocation-device and whole-pool coverage properties of each
pool rather than global state. Let an opt-in QSEECom child bind the two
reserved heaps, register their complete bridges, and route only QSEECom
listener, command, and image-staging allocations through them. Global SCM
keeps its proven per-allocation SHM Bridge path.

The device-tree contract is opt-in, so other platforms retain their existing
allocation behavior.
